Subject: [PATCH] spu: crt1 — pass the fourth lv2 SPU thread argument to main

An lv2 SPU thread (sys_spu_thread_initialize / sysSpuThreadInitialize)
starts with the four 64-bit words of its sys_spu_thread_argument in $3,
$4, $5 and $6.  libgloss's crt1.o was written for Linux libspe2, where
$6 carries the effective address of the SPU's local store: it saves
only $3-$5 in $80-$82, calls main with three arguments and stores $6
into __ea_local_store.  A four-argument main therefore read whatever
_init and atexit left in $6.

Save $6 in $83 (callee-saved, like $80-$82) and pass it to main as the
fourth argument.  This matches the PS3 SDK's own SPU thread entry,
which hands main all four registers unchanged.

__ea_local_store: the SDK's entry does not define or set it at all.
We keep the symbol, because GCC's __ea address-space conversions and
libgcc's __ea software cache (cachemgr.c) reference it, but crt1.o now
stores 0 there instead of the fourth argument.  With 0, a local-store
pointer converted to __ea is the LS offset itself, and the cache
treats EAs in [0, 256K) as local store, so the conversion round-trips;
storing the thread argument would instead make the cache shadow an
arbitrary 256K window of real EA space with local store.  crt2.o
(_STD_MAIN, the libspe2 spulet entry) is unchanged.

diff --color -ruN a/libgloss/spu/crt0.S b/libgloss/spu/crt0.S
--- a/libgloss/spu/crt0.S
+++ b/libgloss/spu/crt0.S
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@
  * The crt1.o prepares the entry for an SPU module. The main() function
  * is called with different parameter list: spu_id, param and env 
  * are passed by R3, R4 and R5 respectively.
+ *
+ * PS3 lv2: an SPU thread receives the four 64-bit arguments of its
+ * sys_spu_thread_argument in R3, R4, R5 and R6, so crt1.o passes all
+ * four to main().  R6 is not the local store EA there, so crt1.o sets
+ * __ea_local_store to 0 instead of storing R6 into it.
  */
 
 #ifdef _STD_MAIN
@@ -57,8 +62,18 @@
 .type _start, @function
 	
 _start:
+#ifdef _STD_MAIN
 	/* Save the local store base from $6.  */
 	stqr $6, __ea_local_store
+#else
+	/* lv2 passes the fourth thread argument in $6, not the local
+	 * store EA.  Zero __ea_local_store: LS-to-__ea conversions then
+	 * yield the LS offset itself, which the __ea cache maps straight
+	 * back to local store, and no real EA range is shadowed.
+	 */
+	il	$7, 0
+	stqr	$7, __ea_local_store
+#endif
 
 #ifdef _STD_MAIN
 	/* 
@@ -98,13 +113,14 @@
 #endif
 
 	/* Save parameter list of main function to the non-volatile
-	 * registers. spu_thread module has three parameters, while
+	 * registers. spu_thread module has four parameters, while
 	 * spulet only has two.
 	 */
 	ori     $80, $3, 0
 	ori     $81, $4, 0
 #ifndef _STD_MAIN
 	ori 	$82, $5, 0
+	ori 	$83, $6, 0
 #endif
 
 	/* The Link Register is initialized to NULL.
@@ -172,6 +188,7 @@
 	ori     $4,$81,0	
 #ifndef _STD_MAIN
 	ori	$5,$82,0
+	ori	$6,$83,0
 #endif
 
 	/* Call the programs main.
